# Reference validation plan — development BLOCKED

Personally read main PDF pp2–4 and visually checked p6. Table 1 identifies CCDC 2445596, P21/c, Z=4 and the cell; section 3.2 gives a symmetry-coded ring contact. These measurements do not determine all atomic positions or molecular neighbors.

Personally read SI pp1–4: it is a checkCIF/PLATON report, with 0 A/B alerts, 3 C and 6 G alerts. It contains neither the full fractional-coordinate loop nor a recoverable source CIF. CCDC access returned an HTML validation/CAPTCHA page, not a CIF. Local CIF search yielded no authenticated 2445596 object.

## Reusable evidence and limits

Old isolated orbitals and conformer logs may test the molecular graph/software, but cannot validate crystal contacts or new dimer energies. The old gap target/tolerance are retired. Source contact percentages are author-derived analyses, held private rather than presented as blind targets.

## Explicit missing prerequisites

- Authenticated CCDC 2445596 CIF and complete fractional atom/occupancy/symmetry data are not available.
- Correct symmetry-inequivalent neighbor inventory and graph mapping cannot be generated without that CIF.
- No representative pair area/interaction-energy pilot or full expanded references exist.

## Minimum pilot and release sequence

1. Obtain the actual deposition through a permitted CCDC/publisher access route, hash it, check DOI/deposition/formula/cell and inspect disorder/occupancy/quality alerts. A downloaded checkCIF or HTML page is not sufficient.
2. Rebuild full molecules and neighbors, establish a bijective label map and normalize H consistently; review symmetry/multiplicity against source packing.
3. Demonstrate one real pair with converged surface area and frozen-geometry CP energies through Gaussian/ORCA or an equivalent calibrated method.
4. Complete all primary pairs plus the specified cutoff and decisive sensitivity controls; freeze numerical intervals from actual evidence; then review release readiness and run independent AR/PR checks.

## Full expanded reference

All primary true neighbors with molecule-resolved area/type data and frozen own/ghost energy terms; area-versus-energy pair comparisons, closest-contact cross-check and cutoff sensitivity. SAPT is optional and no missing decomposition term is a core failure.

## Software and quantitative calibration

Gaussian/ORCA are allowed native energy backends. Psi4 SAPT is optional. A reproducible promolecular/Hirshfeld area implementation must be separately demonstrated using allowed Python/density data; do not assume CrystalExplorer is installed or replace area by contact counts. Numerical uncertainty must be measured from converged raw calculations, model variation and geometry sensitivity. Paper numbers remain historical anchors only; there is no newly calibrated absolute tolerance, ranking or winner. Do not impose optional extensions as gates.

## Actual work in this upgrade

No new quantum, periodic or transport engine was launched. Local source reading, graph/stoichiometry checks and schema tests are development work. Preserve inputs, failed/restarted jobs, actual engine launches, CPU allocation and engine times when a future pilot is authorized and budgeted. Current scope is a development package, not a released benchmark or validated scientific reference.
